text	I read the 30 Oct letter and compared it with the 3 open issues (#12, #13, #14). The main difference is the rate change: the letter and #12 say opposite things.  **1. Rate change: #12 contradicts the letter** - **Letter:** a new rate applies only to customers the partner brings after the change. Current customers keep their commissions as they are. - **#12:** adds a dialog with two options, and the default is **"All customers"**. Its acceptance test expects all 3 existing customers to pay the partner 7% after the change. - **Why they differ:** #12 is based on a decision of 29 Oct, which says the client "no longer has to answer our question 1". The client answered it one day later, on 30 Oct, and chose the other way. - **What is open:** two things need a decision. Either drop the dialog and always apply the new rate to new customers only, or keep the dialog with "New customers only" as the default. In both cases, #12's "Why" text and its acceptance test are now wrong.  **2. Payouts: they match** - The letter says payouts stay monthly, on the 5th. #13 assumes the same thing and only adds the next payout date to the partner page. No conflict.  **3. Rate history: only partly covered** - **Letter:** the client wants to see each rate change in the partner's history. - **Open issues:** only #12 touches this, and it records only which option the merchant chose in the dialog. No issue covers a history entry for every rate change, with the old rate, the new rate and the date. If #12 loses its dialog, nothing covers point 3 at all.  **Not in the letter:** #14 (CSV export of a month's commissions) has nothing to do with the letter. No conflict.  I did not edit or file anything, because the conflict in point 1 is your decision. When you decide, I can rewrite #12 and file a separate issue for the rate history.
