text	#12 is not busy. Your decision makes its default and its acceptance test false, so I correct it now.
Bash	f=$(mktemp); cat > "$f" <<'EOF'; **What.** When the merchant changes the rate of a partner who has customers, a dialog asks where the new rate applies:; ; - **New customers only** (selected by default): the current customers keep their rate; only customers brought from now on pay the new rate.; - **All customers**: every current customer of the partner pays the new rate from the next payment.; ; The partner's history records the choice.; ; **Why.** The client answered our question 1 of 23 Oct in the letter of 30 Oct (`docs/letters/2026-10-30-client.md`): a new rate applies only to customers that the partner brings after the change. Decided on 6 Nov 2026: "New customers only" is the default, and "All customers" stays a choice in the dialog. This replaces the decision of 29 Oct, which made "All customers" the default.; ; **Acceptance.** A partner has 3 customers at 5%. The merchant sets 7% and keeps the default: the 3 customers still pay the partner 5%, and a customer brought after the change pays 7%. With "All customers", the next payment of each of the 3 customers pays the partner 7%.; EOF; gh issue edit 12 --title "Let the merchant choose whether a new partner rate applies to existing customers (default: new customers only)" --body-file "$f" && gh issue comment 12 --body "Default changed to \"New customers only\", after the client's letter of 30 Oct; \"All customers\" stays a choice in the dialog (decided 6 Nov 2026)."; rm "$f"
text	Here is the paragraph for the reply:  > **1. Change of a partner's rate.** Thank you for your answer. We will do it as you describe. By default, a new rate applies only to customers that the partner brings after the change. The commissions on the current customers stay as they are. When the merchant changes a partner's rate, a dialog also offers a second choice, "All customers". With it, the current customers of the partner also pay the new rate, starting from their next payment. The merchant uses this choice only on purpose, and the partner's history shows which choice was made.  I also corrected issue #12, because your decision made parts of it false: - "New customers only" is now the default, and "All customers" is the other choice. - The "Why" now points to the client's letter of 30 Oct and to your decision of 6 Nov. It replaces the old decision of 29 Oct. - The acceptance test is rewritten to match the new default. - The title now says the default. - I added a one-line comment on #12 that says what changed and why.  One gap is still open from point 3 of the letter. #12 only records which choice the merchant made in the dialog. No issue covers a history entry for every rate change, with the old rate, the new rate and the date. If you want, I can file it, or add it to #12.
